{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966796,"nonce":"1C4Mw3i3YHTMZlvVn6CsYaYdDXY=","title":"blinc_node_editor node title drifts down as content body grows — centered on full bounds","message":"In `blinc_node_editor::render::draw_node_title`, the no-subtitle/no-icon branch centered the title at `bounds.y() + bounds.height() * 0.5` — the FULL node bounds. For a schema-driven / content node (`with_content_size`), the body grows the node, so `bounds.height()` grows and the title slides downward as content layout changes. Symptom: \"config title keeps moving when content layout changes.\"\n\n**Why:** `header_y_shift` (render.rs ~374) is correctly 0 for content nodes (`slots.body.height() \u003e 0`), so the header pins to the top — but the no-subtitle/no-icon title path ignored the header band entirely and centered in full bounds.\n\n**How to apply:** Center the title against the fixed-height HEADER band: `header_rect.y() + header_y_shift + header_rect.height() * 0.5` (where `header_rect = translate_rect(slots.header, origin)`). This pins the title for content nodes AND preserves the content-less centering case (when `header_y_shift` centers the header, `header_top + shift + header_h/2 == bounds centre`). The with-subtitle and with-icon branches were already correct (they use `slots.title`/`slots.icon` + `header_y_shift`). `slots.body.height()` is FIXED at the `with_content_size` declared height (taffy `Dimension::Length`), never 0 for content nodes. See feedback signal subtree not full tree.","files":null}]}